  Slug: demagogue-s-calling
  DisplayName: Demagogue's Calling
  IconPath: icons/environment/people/cleric-grey.webp
  Description: Words flow freely from a font within your soul. When you attempt a
    check to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Coerce] or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Make
    an Impression], you can spend a Mythic Point to attempt the check at mythic proficiency.
    The first time each day that you critically succeed on a check to Coerce a creature
    who isn't your ally, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Create a Diversion]
    using your words, or Make an Impression on an indifferent or unfriendly audience,
    you regain a Mythic Point. Edicts tell stories to audiences who have never heard
    them before, use words rather than weapons to resolve conflicts Anathema interrupt
    someone telling a story, resort to violent action without trying to defuse the
    situation with your words
